# Clean Code and Structure

- Keep changes focused; do not refactor unrelated areas.
- Prefer small, composable modules with clear names and single responsibility.
- Remove dead code and avoid duplicated logic.
- Favor explicit error handling and user-safe fallbacks.
- Keep folder structure predictable:
  - Product-level docs at repository root or `docs/`
  - **Mobile** app (React Native) in `mobile/` (legacy folder name `Frontend/` until renamed)
  - **Admin web** in `admin-frontend/` (rename to `frontend/` after `Frontend/` → `mobile/` on Windows — see `PROJECT-SPEC.md` §0)
  - **Backend** in `Backend/` (or `backend/` if aligned with local naming)
  - Feature documentation in `docs/features/<feature-slug>/`
- Every implemented feature must map to a documented acceptance criterion.
